# Sloper environment template for running sloper and sloper-web from this
# checkout.
#
# Copy it next to this file and fill in the values:
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# Nothing reads .env automatically; export it into the shell that starts the
# binary (it is a plain shell file):
#     set -a; . ./.env; set +a
#     ./dist/sloper
#
# .env is gitignored. Never commit real tokens.
# Deploying with Docker instead? Use setup/.env.example, which compose.yml loads.
#
# ── GitHub ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Token for every gh CLI call sloper makes (issues, comments, PRs).
# `gh auth token` prints the token of the account you are logged in as.
GH_TOKEN=""

# Login sloper posts as. Comments by this user count as sloper's own and are
# not answered again.
GH_USERNAME=""

# Commit author for the work sloper pushes. Optional locally, where git's own
# user.name/user.email apply; the Docker setup (setup/script.sh) uses it.
GH_EMAIL=""

# ── Agent (pi) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Model to drive, in pi's "provider/id" form, e.g.
# "anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-20250514" or "openai/gpt-4o:high" (":high" sets
# thinking). Required.
AGENT_MODEL=""

# Key passed to pi as --api-key. Required unless pi already finds the provider's
# own variable (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, OPENAI_API_KEY, ...) in its environment.
AGENT_KEY=""

# Provider name ("anthropic", "openai", "google", "openrouter", ...). Optional
# when the provider is already part of AGENT_MODEL.
AGENT_PROVIDER=""

# Reserved: a custom API base URL is not wired up yet.
AGENT_API=""

# ── Storage (optional, defaults shown) ───────────────────────────────
# SQLite file holding issues, runs, PRs and the audit log.
# SLOPER_DB_PATH="$HOME/.sloper/sloper.sqlite"
# Where pi writes the session transcripts read by the console's Sessions view.
# SLOPER_SESSION_DIR="$HOME/.sloper/sessions"
# Where per-issue git worktrees are created.
# SLOPER_WORKTREE_DIR="$HOME/.sloper/worktrees"

# ── Dashboard API, sloper-web (optional, defaults shown) ─────────────
# SLOPER_WEB_ADDR="127.0.0.1"
# SLOPER_WEB_PORT="8080"
# Require "Authorization: Bearer <token>" on every API route.
# SLOPER_WEB_TOKEN=""
# Repo name reported to the console; defaults to the git remote.
# SLOPER_REPO=""

# ── Repo controller, sloper-controller (optional) ────────────────────
# The controller is the multi-repo backend: attach a repo link and it starts one
# docker container for that repo, running the sloper image built by
# `make build-docker`. It inherits GH_TOKEN, GH_USERNAME, GH_EMAIL, AGENT_MODEL,
# AGENT_KEY, AGENT_PROVIDER and SLOPER_WEB_TOKEN from this shell, so a repo
# container can clone the repo and run the agent.
#
# Serve the controller API (the console's "New repo" button talks to it):
#     make run-controller
#
# SLOPER_CONTROLLER_ADDR="127.0.0.1"
# SLOPER_CONTROLLER_PORT="9090"
# Require "Authorization: Bearer <token>" on every controller route. Set this
# whenever the controller is reachable from anywhere but your own machine.
# SLOPER_CONTROLLER_TOKEN=""
# Controller registry (attached repos, ports, container ids). Keep it separate
# from a repo instance's SLOPER_DB_PATH.
# SLOPER_CONTROLLER_DB_PATH="$HOME/.sloper/controller.sqlite"
# SLOPER_CONTROLLER_LOG_DIR="$HOME/.sloper/controller-logs"
# How often the controller reconciles containers (seconds).
# SLOPER_CONTROLLER_RECONCILE_SECONDS="10"
#
# Image every repo container runs. Build it with `make build-docker`.
# SLOPER_IMAGE="sloper-agent:latest"
# Host port range handed out, one port per repo, for that repo's sloper-web.
# SLOPER_PORT_RANGE="8080-8180"
# Host address those ports are published on, and the hostname the console should
# use to reach them. Use 0.0.0.0 when the console runs on another machine.
# SLOPER_PUBLISH_ADDR="127.0.0.1"
# SLOPER_PUBLIC_HOST="localhost"
# Optional docker network for repo containers.
# SLOPER_NETWORK=""
# SLOPER_RESTART_POLICY="unless-stopped"

# ── Console pointing at the controller (build-time) ──────────────────
# Default controller URL the "Repositories" page starts with. The console also
# lets you change it in the UI, per browser.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SLOPER_CONTROLLER_URL="http://localhost:9090"
